<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoDeepCopy - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/godeepcopy/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/godeepcopy/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 188</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_188/</link><pubDate>Mon, 17 Feb 2025 23:43:08 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_188/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Discuss the process of slice copying.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="go-slices-are-divided-into-shallow-copy-and-deep-copy"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Go slices are divided into shallow copy and deep copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#go-slices-are-divided-into-shallow-copy-and-deep-copy" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 class="heading-element" id="shallow-copy"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Shallow Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#shallow-copy" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;A Go slice consists of length, capacity, and an underlying array. A shallow copy only duplicates the slice header (slice pointer, length, and capacity).&#10;Since the underlying array of slices is shared, modifying slice elements will affect other slices.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 101</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_101/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:42:39 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_101/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; var a = [5]int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}&#10; var r [5]int&#10;&#10; for i, v := range a {&#10; if i == 0 {&#10; a[1] = 12&#10; a[2] = 13&#10; }&#10; r[i] = v&#10; }&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;r = &amp;#34;, r)&#10; fmt.Println(&amp;#34;a = &amp;#34;, a)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;r = [1 2 3 4 5]&#10;a = [1 12 13 4 5]&#10;The range expression participates in the loop with a copy, meaning that in the example, a copy of &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; is used in the loop, not the actual &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>